<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov pork imports rise 29.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov pork imports rise 29.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in November rose 29.6 percent to 31,399 tonnes from 24,229 tonnes a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Nov 96	Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	     31,399	 41,751	 24,229</p>
<p> Refrigerated    11,863	 15,404	 11,361</p>
<p> Frozen	    19,536	 26,347	 12,868</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     5,208	  7,284	  3,959</p>
<p> U.S.		 5,634	  6,949	  2,757</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Nov 96	  Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	    12,874	  16,901	  7,431</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in the first 11 months of calendar 1996 totalled 157,251 tonnes, against 155,633 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in the first 11 months of calendar 1996 came to 452,327 tonnes, against 333,646 tonnes in the same period of 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
